Coding app marks

Each file is the maker's own artwork, copied from its official brand or press
page without changing the artwork (fetched 25 Oct 2026). The marks are trademarks of their
owners and are used only to identify each app next to its name. Cua is not
affiliated with or endorsed by any of them. The app shows each mark in its
original colours or in the maker's own one-colour variant, at a fixed aspect
ratio, with clear space around it. Files ending in -dark are the maker's
variant for dark backgrounds and show when the app theme is dark.

mark-cursor.svg, mark-cursor-dark.svg
  Cursor (Anysphere, Inc.): CUBE_2D_LIGHT.svg and CUBE_2D_DARK.svg from the brand assets zip.
  Source: https://cursor.com/brand
  Guideline: use the supplied light or dark variant; refer to the product as "Cursor".

mark-vscode.svg
  Visual Studio Code (Microsoft): vscode.svg from visual-studio-code-icons.zip, used in both themes
  (the white vscode-alt.svg is only for blue backgrounds).
  Source: https://code.visualstudio.com/brand
  Guideline: don't modify, recolour, stretch or add a background; keep clear space of 25% of the "fish".

mark-gemini-cli.svg, mark-gemini-cli-dark.svg
  Gemini CLI (Google): gemini-cli-icon_full-color.svg and gemini-cli-icon_monotone_on_dark.svg.
  Source: https://geminicli.com/brand-kit/
  Guideline: https://geminicli.com/brandassets/gemini_cli_logo_icon_guidelines.pdf (never alter the icon or its gradient).

mark-cline.svg, mark-cline-dark.svg
  Cline (Cline Bot Inc.): General Logos/Bot/SVG/BOT_LIGHT.svg and BOT_DARK.svg from cline-brand-assets.zip.
  Source: https://cline.bot/brand
  Guideline: use the supplied light or dark variants.

mark-opencode.svg, mark-opencode-dark.svg
  OpenCode (Anomaly): opencode-logo-light.svg and opencode-logo-dark.svg from opencode-brand-assets.zip.
  Source: https://opencode.ai/brand
  Guideline: use the supplied light or dark variants.

mark-pi.svg, mark-pi-dark.svg
  Pi (Earendil Inc. & contributors): the press kit's Badge SVG, "square mark for favicons and compact badges"
  (https://pi.dev/favicon.svg). That one file holds both official colours (#111111, and #f6f6f6 under
  prefers-color-scheme: dark); it is split into two files so the app theme, not the OS, picks one.
  Source: https://pi.dev/press-kit (press kit under the MIT License)

mark-windsurf.svg, mark-windsurf-dark.svg
  Windsurf (Cognition AI, Inc.): windsurf-black-symbol.svg and windsurf-white-symbol.svg.
  Source: https://windsurf.com/brand
  Guideline: symbol for space-limited layouts; no outline, effects, gradients, rotation or recolouring; keep contrast and spacing.

mark-copilot.svg, mark-copilot-dark.svg
  GitHub Copilot (GitHub, Inc.): Copilot_Icon_Black.svg and Copilot_Icon_White.svg from GitHub_Logos.zip.
  Source: https://brand.github.com/foundations/logo and https://brand.github.com/brand-identity/copilot
  Guideline: black or white only, no effects, don't distort or alter.

mark-amp.svg
  Amp: app-icon.svg, used in both themes (the press kit has no dark-mode icon; the light glyph carries the contrast).
  Source: https://ampcode.com/press-kit

mark-goose.svg, mark-goose-dark.svg
  goose (Agentic AI Foundation / Block): the black mark, and the desktop app icon (black goose on a white tile) for dark mode.
  Sources: https://github.com/aaif-goose/goose/blob/main/documentation/static/img/goose.svg
           https://github.com/aaif-goose/goose/blob/main/ui/desktop/src/images/icon.svg
  Guideline: none published.

mark-zed.svg, mark-zed-dark.svg
  Zed (Zed Industries, Inc.): the logomark in pure black and pure white, from the page's "Copy SVG"
  (a height attribute added so the file stands alone).
  Source: https://zed.dev/brand
  Guideline: black, white or brand blue only; don't recolour or distort; no implied endorsement.

mark-antigravity.svg
  Google Antigravity (Google): antigravity-icon__full-color.svg, used in both themes.
  Source: https://antigravity.google/press

mark-claude.svg
  Claude Code (Anthropic): Claude Spark - Clay.svg from the press kit, the only colour the spark is issued in;
  used in both themes (2.9:1 on the light onboarding background, 3.1:1 on the white tile, 5.6:1 on dark).
  Source: https://www.anthropic.com/press-kit

mark-openai.svg, mark-openai-dark.svg
  OpenAI Codex (OpenAI): OAI_OpenAI-Blossom_Black.svg and OAI_OpenAI-Blossom_White.svg from openai-logos.zip
  (https://cdn.openai.com/brand/openai-logos.zip). The files keep OpenAI's built-in clear space; the app scales the
  image so the Blossom matches the other marks.
  Source: https://openai.com/brand/
  Guideline: use as provided, no added colours or effects, keep clear space; no implied endorsement.

mark-hermes.svg, mark-hermes-dark.svg
  Hermes (Nous Research): assets/nous-girl-black.svg and assets/nous-girl-white.svg.
  Source: https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/tree/main/assets
  Guideline: none published.

mark-openclaw.svg
  OpenClaw: the static lobster mark served as https://openclaw.ai/favicon.svg, used in both themes
  (no dark variant is published; the project's own dark UI uses the same mark).
  Source: https://openclaw.ai/press (no published logo guide; press@openclaw.org)

No usable official mark (letter tile):
  Kiro (Amazon): no brand or press kit at https://kiro.dev; AWS marks need permission.
